<title>USA: TABLE--Kimberly Q2 oper shr $0.60 vs $0.56.</title>
<headline>TABLE--Kimberly Q2 oper shr $0.60 vs $0.56.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q2 ended June 30	 1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.65		    $0.64</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.60		    $0.56</p>
<p> Net			  363.5		    364.7</p>
<p> Revs		     3,124.3		  3,347.7</p>
<p> Shrs oustanding	  559.3		    563.3</p>
<p>6 Mos ended June 30</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.31		    $1.20</p>
<p> Net			  732.5		    679.5</p>
<p> Revs		     6,361.9		  6,549.8</p>
<p> Avg			  560.1		    564.0</p>
<p>(All data above in millions except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Kimberly-Clark Corp</p>
<p>Q2 1997 includes net non-operating gain of $16.3 million, or $0.03 a share, related to sale of Regio Tissue business by Kimberly-Clark de Mexico SA de CV.</p>
<p>1997 Q2 includes additional extraordinary gain of $12.7 million, or $0.02 a share, from its selling a 50.1-percent owned Canadian tissue subsidiary in June.</p>
<p>Q2 1997 and 1996 are as of the end of the period, while for the six months results oustanding shares are averaged.</p>
